  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Jesuit AIDS Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project targets young people, aged between 12-19 years, in and around Harare, aiming by 2003:
1) To increase the level of HIV/AIDS information and knowledge among young people in schools and youth clubs at colleges and parishes.
2) To influence positive behaviour practices relevant to preventing the spread of HIV among young people in and out of schools, youth clubs, colleges and parishes.
3) To reduce stigma attached to HIV/AIDS, impart knowledge of right relationships, life skills (eg. negotiation skills, assertiveness, problem solving, self awareness, communication) and gender sensitivity among young people
4) 	To increase the level of community/institutional support for young people to effectively participate in their own HIV/AIDS/STI prevention and care initiatives.</narrative>
  </description>
